  "description": "Republic of Ireland District Electoral Divisions/Wards as at 1931-04-01, assembled from Connacht (= 1919 boundaries), Leinster 1931, Munster (= 1921 boundaries), Ulster (= 1921 boundaries). Modified version of District Electoral Divisions/Wards 1936. In 1936, Dublin county borough’s wards were modified. 14 of the existing 20 wards remained the same, 2 of them were split in 2 and the other 4 were expanded. The DEDs of Pembroke East, Pembroke West (previously wards of Pembroke Township) and Rathmines and Rathgar West (previously a ward of Rathmines & Rathgar Township) were converted into wards. The DED of Rathmines and Rathgar East (previously a ward of Rathmines and Rathgar Township) was converted into a ward and expanded. With 7 brand new wards being formed, the total number of wards was increased to 33. The 2 DEDs of Glasnevin Rural and Donnybrook were fully absorbed while the 7 DEDs of Castleknock, Drumcondra Rural, Finglas, Howth Rural, Palmerston, Rathfarnham and Terenure were reduced in size.",
